Path and text compose by first retrieving the value at the specified path and then extracting the text content from that value. The `path` function traverses the object structure, and `text` converts the resulting value into a string.

```sol
let result = path ["user", "name"] (JObj [("user", JStr "Alice")]);
let name = text result;
```

Source: fprisc/sol/lib/json.sol
